{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.AdelicReebRestrictedProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.AdelicReebRestrictedProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.adelic_reeb_squeeze_local_to_global","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.adelic_reeb_squeeze_local_to_global","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-reeb-restricted-product.lean#L71-L83","doc":"**Local-to-global surreal squeeze.** If the local order of `a` weakly\ndominates that of `b` at every active place, and *strictly* dominates at\nsome place `v₀`, then the global order of `a` strictly dominates that of\n`b`. Applied with `a = δ²·ε⁻¹`, `b = ε³` and the per-place squeeze\n(`lem:surreal-squeeze` at each `v`), this gives the global adelic squeeze\n`ordw_𝔸(δ²·ε⁻¹) > ordw_𝔸(ε³)` of `rem:adelic-tate-squeeze`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.adelic_reeb_order_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.adelic_reeb_order_additive","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-reeb-restricted-product.lean#L62-L69","doc":"**Tate factorisation / additivity.** The global `ω`-order of a product is\nthe sum of the local `ω`-orders of its factors. Multiplicativity of the\nadelic observable corresponds to pointwise addition of local orders. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:adelic-reeb-restricted-product","label":"prop:adelic-reeb-restricted-product","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-reeb-restricted-product.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.globalOrd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.globalOrd","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-reeb-restricted-product.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The global `ω`-order of an adelic observable, as the finite sum of its\nlocal `ω`-orders over the set `S` of active places (restricted-product\ncondition: only finitely many places are active). `ord v` is the local\n`ordw_v`; `Γ` is the common value group (the `ω`-grade of `𝐍𝐨`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}